          "text": "Cyclical premenstrual symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For years, regular 28-day cycles with 5–6 days of moderate bleeding. 7–10 days before menses: marked irritability, mood swings, increased anxiety, feeling unable to cope, bloating, breast tenderness, and headaches. Symptoms resolve 2–3 days after bleeding starts; patient reports being pretty normal mid-cycle. Symptoms make her snappy with her partner and work harder, but she continues working full-time."
      }
